---
import StoryLayout from '../layouts/StoryLayout.astro';
import StoryArt from '../components/StoryArt.astro';
import AgentMeta from '../components/AgentMeta.astro';
const siteOrigin = import.meta.env.FROGLET_SITE_ORIGIN || 'https://froglet.dev';
const prompt = `Help me share a small dataset or tool with Froglet. Read ${new URL('/publish/agent.md', siteOrigin)}. First ask what I want to share and who should be able to use it. Use the configured Froglet tool or a verified installation. Explain the supported access controls and their limits. Propose the smallest useful selection, show what is included and omitted, prepare a separate snapshot or function, and verify an example through Froglet itself. Keep credentials and confidential material out of public metadata and examples. Ask me separately before persistent installation and before publishing the exact package and access settings. Start free. Preserve my existing files and agent settings. Report local verification, public reachability, and recipient execution separately.`;
---
<StoryLayout title="Share something useful · Froglet" description="Prepare your first Froglet service with your AI assistant. Choose what to share, see an example, and approve before publishing." path="/publish/">
<AgentMeta slot="head" route="publish" />
<div class="story-wrap">
  <section class="story-hero story-hero--compact"><div class="story-hero__copy"><span class="story-kicker">Your first service</span><h1>Start with something <span class="story-accent">small and useful.</span></h1><p class="story-lede">A research table. A product catalog. A calculation you repeat. Your AI assistant helps turn it into something another person can use.</p><div class="story-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#start">Get the setup prompt</a><a class="btn secondary" href="#walkthrough">See the steps</a></div><p class="story-note">Public beta · Start free · Runs on your computer</p></div><StoryArt name="02-walkthrough-choose" eager alt="Bob chooses a few useful cards from a larger collection." /></section>

  <section class="story-section story-split" id="start"><div><span class="story-kicker">Start with your assistant</span><h2>You describe it.<br />Your assistant prepares it.</h2><ol class="story-start"><li><strong>Open Codex or Claude Code.</strong>Use a project where the assistant can read the file you want to share.</li><li><strong>Pick a small first example.</strong>A spreadsheet exported as CSV, a JSON or SQLite catalog, or a small function.</li><li><strong>Paste these instructions.</strong>Your assistant should show a preview before asking to publish.</li></ol><p class="story-note">The native setup supports Apple Silicon macOS and Linux x86_64/arm64. A chat-only assistant cannot run this workflow. <a href="/learn/quickstart/">Read the setup guide</a>.</p></div><div class="story-prompt"><label for="publisher-prompt">Instructions for your assistant</label><textarea id="publisher-prompt" readonly rows="12">{prompt}</textarea><div class="story-actions"><button id="copy-publisher-prompt" class="btn primary" type="button">Copy setup prompt</button><a href="/publish/agent.md">Read the full instructions</a></div><p id="publisher-copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div></section>

  <section class="story-section" id="walkthrough"><div class="story-heading"><span class="story-kicker">You make the decisions</span><h2>Four moments.<br />No surprise publication.</h2></div><div class="story-grid story-grid--two">
    <article class="story-step"><StoryArt name="02-walkthrough-choose" /><span class="story-kicker">01 / Choose</span><h3>Decide what leaves your desk.</h3><p>Your assistant proposes useful fields or a small operation. You see what will be included and omitted. The original files stay intact.</p></article>
    <article class="story-step"><StoryArt name="03-walkthrough-preview" /><span class="story-kicker">02 / Preview</span><h3>Try a real example.</h3><p>The selected package is tested locally through Froglet. Review its result and the exact information it exposes.</p></article>
    <article class="story-step"><StoryArt name="04-walkthrough-publish" /><span class="story-kicker">03 / Approve</span><h3>Publish the version you reviewed.</h3><p>Installation and publication are separate decisions. Check the package, public example, access settings, limits, and free price before approving.</p></article>
    <article class="story-step"><StoryArt name="05-walkthrough-share" width={1536} height={1024} /><span class="story-kicker">04 / Share</span><h3>Send a link. Let someone use it.</h3><p>The recipient’s assistant checks the service and makes its own call. If it requires an invitation, send the access file separately through a trusted channel. The link alone does not grant access.</p></article>
  </div></section>

  <section class="story-section story-split"><StoryArt name="08-own-your-service" alt="Bob looks after the service running on his own computer." /><div><span class="story-kicker">After you publish</span><h2>It still belongs<br />on your terms.</h2><ul class="story-checks"><li><strong>Keep the host running.</strong><span>Your computer needs to stay awake and online. Managed always-on hosting is outside this release.</span></li><li><strong>Review every new version.</strong><span>Changed source files need a new preview and approval. Nothing is republished automatically.</span></li><li><strong>Pause when you need to.</strong><span>Your assistant can pause, resume, restore a validated version, or unpublish. Ask it to “Open Froglet status” to check health.</span></li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="story-section"><div class="story-callout"><h3>A good first experiment</h3><p>Use a small, non-confidential example. This is a public beta: clean-machine and first-time-user qualification are still pending. Verify the immutable release before installing, and review the exact public material before publishing.</p><p><a href="/learn/share-services/">Full sharing and invitation guide</a> · <a href="/learn/provider-onboarding/">Advanced functions, payments, and hosting</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="story-closing"><h2>Prefer to look around first?</h2><p>Browse services or inspect a signed sample in your browser.</p><div class="story-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/marketplace/">Explore services</a><a class="btn secondary" href="/verify-receipt/">Inspect a sample record</a></div></section>
</div>
<script>
const prompt = document.getElementById('publisher-prompt') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
const status = document.getElementById('publisher-copy-status')!;
document.getElementById('copy-publisher-prompt')!.addEventListener('click', async () => {
  try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(prompt.value); status.textContent = 'Prompt copied. Paste it into your assistant.'; }
  catch { prompt.focus(); prompt.select(); status.textContent = 'Select and copy the prompt above using your device’s copy command.'; }
});
</script>
</StoryLayout>
